From 81bd49b793451e15b098a1622b1b06c0c4453b29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:26:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] grid: stop growing tracks that already reached their limit

distribute_space_up_to_limits() computed each iteration's increase from
the distance between a track's base size and its limit without counting
the increase already incurred in earlier iterations, and then applied that
increase to every affected track, including ones frozen at their limit.
With minmax(0, 756px) minmax(0, 316px) in a 936px wide grid, the second
iteration handed the remaining 304px to both tracks, giving 620px/620px
where the spec (and Chrome) freeze the second track at 316px and give the
first 620px.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
